<title>USA: Minnesota livestock flood losses near 10,000--FSA.</title>
<headline>Minnesota livestock flood losses near 10,000--FSA.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Livestock losses in Minnesota have reached around 10,000 head following extensive flooding in the Red River Valley, a spokesman for the Minnesota Farm Service Agency (FSA) said.</p>
<p>The total included about 5,000 beef cows, 1,000 dairy cows, 2,500 hogs and around 1,000 sheep, he added.</p>
<p>The spokesman said the loss estimate was preliminary and more exact numbers would be available at a later date.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408 8720))</p>
